# Atomic writes leave a .tmp beside their target for a few milliseconds.
#
# That is long enough. `git add web/data` walks tens of thousands of paths and
# takes seconds over it; if it decides to index one of these and the rename
# takes it away first, git exits 128 — and under `bash -e` that ends a
# five-and-a-half-hour collection window. It happened four times in three days
# and showed up in the Actions tab as three grey rows and the string
# "exit code 128".
#
# The rule covers directories as well as files, which is why the room-snapshot
# builder stages its new set as `room-snapshots.tmp` before swapping it in:
# one rule, rather than a second one somebody has to remember.
*.tmp
